/datum/lore/character_background/religion/species/scori/buriedones
	name = "Buried Ones"
	id = "religion_scori_buriedones"
	category = "Scorian"
	desc = "Akin to local animistic spirits, the buried ones embody specific geographic features such as volcanoes, canyons \
	and cliffs. While belief in and prayers to the buried ones are common, scorians who feel a particularly strong connection \
	to their home, favorite hunting ground, trade route, etc. might choose to focus more on offerings to the buried ones that \
	inhabit those places rather than the broader portfolio the Mother represents."

/datum/lore/character_background/religion/species/scori/mother
	name = "Mother"
	id = "religion_scori_mother"
	category = "Scorian"
	desc = "While most scorians acknowledge and will even pray to and give thanks to the buried ones, a henotheistic \
	reverance to Mother is extremely common. Regarded as the personification of Surt itself, it isn't \
	difficult to see why this would be the case. She is seen as a nurturing and protective figure, whose gifts of lead, \
	copper and other minerals are used in many applications. Meanwhile goliaths and gutshanks, whose meat, bones, hides and \
	carapaces are utterly essential to scorian society, are regarded as her children in equal measure to the scorians themselves."

/datum/lore/character_background/religion/species/scori/father
	name = "Father"
	id = "religion_scori_father"
	category = "Scorian"
	desc = "A loose conglomeration of heretical fringe beliefs, some scorians venerate the Father who is otherwise shunned \
	by most as an agent of chaos and corruption. Scorians who revere the Father tend to have a more nuanced view \
	of Mother and the buried ones, seeing both good and bad qualities in those who are otherwise seen as entirely benevolent or malevolent. \
	This also applies to the Father himself, who is sometimes interpreted by those who worship him as something like a trickster deity, \
	testing and pushing scorians into danger for their own edification."
